# ── Local Supabase testing overrides ─────────────────────────────
# Copy the relevant lines into .env.local (main app) and admin/.env.local
# to point the website-DB clients at the LOCAL Supabase stack started by
# scripts/local-db/setup.sh. Leave these UNSET in Vercel — production
# falls back to the hardcoded website-project values.
#
# The anon/service keys below are the supabase CLI's well-known local
# development keys (printed by `supabase start` / `supabase status`).
# They are NOT secrets — they only work against your local Docker stack.

# Main app (.env.local) — website-DB override:
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBSITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBSITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key from `supabase status`>
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service_role key from `supabase status`>

# Admin app (admin/.env.local) — admin is fully env-driven already:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key from `supabase status`>
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service_role key from `supabase status`>
#
# NOTE (admin login): admin auth checks admin_users against the LOCAL db.
# scripts/local-db/seed.sql creates a local auth user
# admin@local.test / password "localadmin" and inserts it into admin_users.

# Stripe — ALWAYS test keys locally (repo history has sk_live keys; never
# run local checkout tests against those):
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...   (from `stripe listen`)

# Mobile project vars stay as-is (auth reads only).
